WEBVTT

00:06.548 --> 00:10.218
[sweet airy music]

00:43.043 --> 00:45.503
[soft gentle music]

00:50.967 --> 00:55.221
[Yeon-su] They say that the more
that you try and run away from the past,

00:56.055 --> 00:58.850
conversely the more
you eventually become trapped in it.

01:00.560 --> 01:03.104
[soft gentle music]

01:07.817 --> 01:11.738
Yeon-su's grandmother picks her up
because she doesn't have any parents.

01:11.821 --> 01:13.865
Why don't you have any parents, Yeon-su?

01:13.948 --> 01:15.700
You know that means
you can't play house with us.

01:19.370 --> 01:20.914
Who says I wanna play house with you?

01:24.209 --> 01:25.627
[Yeon-su] Makes perfect sense.

01:26.461 --> 01:28.379
Why do you care so much about her?

01:28.463 --> 01:30.215
That self-centered princess
doesn't like you,

01:30.298 --> 01:31.591
she doesn't even know you exist.

01:31.674 --> 01:33.051
She's right. Think about it.

01:33.134 --> 01:35.512
Yeon-su's never bothered
treated us or anything.

01:35.595 --> 01:36.971
We always bought her stuff.

01:37.055 --> 01:40.058
Still, it wasn't like she asked us
to buy her any of those things.

01:40.141 --> 01:43.186
It's called being shameless.
She still accepted them every single time.

01:43.269 --> 01:44.771
[Yeon-su] Even after all this time…

01:44.854 --> 01:45.980
[sniffles]

01:46.689 --> 01:48.066
I really wish that…

01:49.442 --> 01:50.652
[soft sob]

01:51.236 --> 01:53.655
I was only poor enough
to the point that I…

01:54.823 --> 01:56.741
I could at least handle it.

01:57.617 --> 01:58.993
…I may look different now…

02:04.624 --> 02:10.672
but I'm still that helpless girl,
lost inside that playground.

02:16.469 --> 02:18.847
Don't know why,
but my life's always been that way.

02:19.973 --> 02:22.016
[fragile music]

02:25.311 --> 02:26.855
[soft sob]

02:32.360 --> 02:33.403
Yeon-su…

02:36.156 --> 02:37.657
Let's stop doing this.

02:43.955 --> 02:45.790
[shaky breathing]

02:51.462 --> 02:53.464
Always worrying about not getting hurt…

02:53.548 --> 02:54.424
I…

02:59.262 --> 03:01.764
…and then ending up
hurting the people I love.

03:01.848 --> 03:03.433
I don't

03:04.100 --> 03:06.477
see the point
in the two of us being together.

03:07.562 --> 03:10.356
All 'cause I had an inferiority complex.

03:10.440 --> 03:12.609
["There For You" by Kim Na Young playing]

03:18.156 --> 03:19.449
Enjoy your food, guys.

03:19.532 --> 03:21.492
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

03:21.576 --> 03:22.744
Hold on a sec.

03:27.290 --> 03:31.669
[Yeon-su] Moving forward
pretending like everything was fine

03:31.753 --> 03:34.923
hanging onto the hope
that things would get better somehow.

03:35.006 --> 03:36.466
And that was when it happened.

03:38.593 --> 03:40.803
["There For You" playing]

03:43.223 --> 03:45.141
INCOMING CALL
CHOI UNG

03:45.934 --> 03:47.560
It seems to be a memory

03:48.144 --> 03:49.479
that Ung doesn't recall.

03:54.150 --> 03:56.027
Ung called me that night.

03:56.110 --> 03:58.279
It was the first time
after we'd broken up.

03:58.363 --> 04:01.115
Just tell me the reason
why we can't be together.

04:01.199 --> 04:02.992
That's all, Yeon-su.

04:09.666 --> 04:12.335
Because if you don't, at least
give me one good reason,

04:13.753 --> 04:17.006
I'm gonna have no choice
but to hate everything about myself.

04:20.885 --> 04:24.305
I'll have to just accept that I'm
someone who deserves to be abandoned.

04:25.223 --> 04:26.557
[shaky breathing]

04:27.517 --> 04:29.477
["There For You" continuing]

04:35.984 --> 04:37.110
[deep exhale]

04:48.955 --> 04:52.166
It's not you, it's me. I'm going through…

04:54.002 --> 04:55.211
a rough patch.

04:56.754 --> 05:00.425
It's just, my family is going
through a tough time.

05:02.260 --> 05:04.137
I can't afford dating right now.

05:05.805 --> 05:07.265
And I don't want you to…

05:08.933 --> 05:13.104
I mean, I don't expect you to
get consumed by all this misery.

05:13.187 --> 05:14.981
[Yeon-su sobs over phone]

05:15.064 --> 05:16.357
That's why.

05:18.151 --> 05:19.402
[scoffs]

05:21.362 --> 05:24.032
[sighs]
Seriously, is that all?

05:25.325 --> 05:26.159
[Ung sighs]

05:29.245 --> 05:32.957
It would have been better to just say
you don't love me anymore or something.

05:34.834 --> 05:36.169
[Ung] Because if that's why…

05:39.380 --> 05:41.632
if that's the reason
you're breaking up with me…

05:44.427 --> 05:45.970
that's just ridiculous.

05:48.306 --> 05:50.892
["There For You" continuing]

06:11.662 --> 06:13.956
Why did we even break up back then?

06:14.582 --> 06:17.877
[Yeon-su] Just like that.
That's what the past does to you.

06:19.462 --> 06:21.255
The more you try to run away from it,

06:21.339 --> 06:25.551
the more it just traps you in.
It'll find you no matter what you do.

06:28.221 --> 06:33.601
And eventually, you'll end up
making the same mistakes.

06:33.684 --> 06:38.773
EPISODE 14
LIFE IS BEAUTIFUL

06:43.945 --> 06:45.655
What's this all of a sudden?

06:46.864 --> 06:48.950
It's just, I've always been curious.

06:50.827 --> 06:54.455
We'd always argue, break up, and then
get back together. Over and over again.

06:54.539 --> 06:56.290
It never bothered me that much…

06:56.374 --> 06:57.291
[Ung scoffs]

06:57.959 --> 07:01.671
…because I always knew that
we'd never break up for real anyway.

07:03.673 --> 07:05.174
Except for that day.

07:06.259 --> 07:07.844
[Ung] I wasn't so sure anymore.

07:08.594 --> 07:12.807
It felt like you were
really desperate to break up with me.

07:16.561 --> 07:20.022
So why? I wanna know the reason.

07:29.949 --> 07:30.825
Back then I…

07:32.160 --> 07:34.036
I was getting very exhausted.

07:34.120 --> 07:38.040
You know how busy I was part-timing,
making ends meet and writing resumes.

07:43.421 --> 07:45.590
What's the point in bringing up the past?

07:45.673 --> 07:47.675
Why don't we just forget about all that?

07:47.758 --> 07:49.635
The only thing that matters
is we're back together.

07:50.595 --> 07:51.721
Hmm.

07:56.476 --> 07:59.061
It's getting late.
I should be getting home now.

07:59.145 --> 08:01.189
Grandma's been upset
'cause I've been coming home late.

08:01.272 --> 08:02.356
She's gonna flip.

08:02.440 --> 08:04.484
- I'll drop you off.
- It's okay. I can just call a cab.

08:04.567 --> 08:07.820
I'll be fine. You just got home.
You need to rest. Get some sleep.

08:09.280 --> 08:10.364
Yeon-su.

08:15.119 --> 08:16.287
Take care, okay?

08:16.913 --> 08:17.997
Hmm.

08:38.309 --> 08:41.437
[gentle vulnerable music]

09:30.653 --> 09:32.196
[sleepy groan]

09:33.990 --> 09:35.116
[Ja-gyeong] You're home.

09:36.409 --> 09:40.079
What about dinner? Have you eaten already?

09:43.082 --> 09:45.668
What's wrong?
Did something bad happen to you?

09:47.128 --> 09:47.962
[exhales sharply]

09:48.045 --> 09:50.715
Nothing. Everything's fine.

09:56.762 --> 09:57.930
Yeon-su…

09:59.890 --> 10:03.144
You know,
that jerk came by the house today.

10:07.231 --> 10:08.065
I know.

10:09.108 --> 10:11.152
Well, I didn't call him. I promise you.

10:11.944 --> 10:13.779
That boy came on his own.

10:14.989 --> 10:16.616
So what did you say to him?

10:17.325 --> 10:19.076
You scold his ears off again?

10:19.577 --> 10:21.120
Of course I didn't.

10:21.203 --> 10:23.956
You think I'm like
some kind of pitbull or something?

10:24.040 --> 10:25.374
[chuckles softly]

10:32.965 --> 10:34.967
[Ja-gyeong] By the way, Yeon-su.

10:35.635 --> 10:37.011
[Yeon-su] Yes?

10:37.094 --> 10:40.222
[Ja-gyeong] Did… I mean,
back then when you broke up with him,

10:41.766 --> 10:46.479
did you… did you break up with him
because of our tough situation?

10:55.863 --> 10:56.989
Huh?

11:00.409 --> 11:01.494
Did you…

11:02.620 --> 11:05.122
break up with him
because you were shouldering

11:05.706 --> 11:08.167
everything by yourself?

11:09.502 --> 11:12.838
What do you mean? Of course not!
Why would you even think that?

11:15.591 --> 11:18.677
We just had a big fight
and then ended things.

11:18.761 --> 11:22.264
Which shouldn't be a surprise, seeing as
I have a nasty temper just like you.

11:28.938 --> 11:31.482
Can you stop
thinking about silly stuff like that?

11:35.528 --> 11:36.821
[Yeon-su groans softly]

11:37.405 --> 11:39.323
This is the warmest spot in the world.

11:40.324 --> 11:44.787
Hey, Grandma, can I sleep here with you?
It's been a while.

11:48.207 --> 11:49.834
[soft caring music]

12:15.025 --> 12:16.068
[sniffs]

12:18.946 --> 12:20.156
[inhales]

12:21.323 --> 12:24.160
If you have something to say,
please, I wanna know.

12:25.453 --> 12:26.704
Uh, sure…

12:28.080 --> 12:32.501
Although, Yeon-su, that girl told me
not to say anything to you.

12:32.585 --> 12:36.005
I'm only telling you this because you
decided to come here on your own.

12:36.088 --> 12:37.131
Okay.

12:38.883 --> 12:41.802
You really like my granddaughter,
don't you?

12:42.636 --> 12:45.181
I can guarantee you,
I like her a lot more than you think.

12:46.223 --> 12:50.060
Okay. Good. Then nothing else matters.

12:51.145 --> 12:53.355
I'm asking you to stand by her,
no matter what.

12:54.482 --> 12:56.859
- But, you don't need to worry about--
- What I mean is,

12:57.443 --> 12:59.737
I want you to be by her side always.

12:59.820 --> 13:02.323
And not just for now,
but as long as you can.

13:02.990 --> 13:05.201
Please don't let
my granddaughter feel alone.

13:06.452 --> 13:08.037
[gentle music]

13:10.706 --> 13:13.250
Ever since Yeon-su was a little girl,

13:13.334 --> 13:15.753
I was the only person
she had that she could rely on.

13:17.588 --> 13:19.423
[Ja-gyeong] It's been a lonely existence

13:19.507 --> 13:22.343
as she had neither
a true family nor friends.

13:22.426 --> 13:23.594
But it didn't matter,

13:23.677 --> 13:26.847
she carried all the burden
all by herself whatever it was.

13:26.931 --> 13:29.808
When our family fell apart
and we had no money to recover,

13:30.434 --> 13:33.062
that young girl
pushed forward single-handedly.

13:37.149 --> 13:39.318
[breathes in shakily]

13:39.401 --> 13:42.905
In any case,
she hasn't had many things in life.

13:43.906 --> 13:47.076
Except you, you've always had
a special place in her heart.

13:48.953 --> 13:51.539
So please don't make her
feel lonely anymore.

13:51.622 --> 13:54.083
Stay by her side
no matter what happens, will you?

13:57.086 --> 13:59.004
Okay. Don't worry, I will.

14:00.548 --> 14:01.882
[sighs in relief]

14:02.633 --> 14:04.718
I know this is a lot for you,

14:05.302 --> 14:08.264
this is a heavy burden
that I'm placing on your shoulders.

14:08.347 --> 14:10.140
But I don't have a choice.

14:11.350 --> 14:13.811
She's suffered so much
and I'm asking for your help

14:13.894 --> 14:15.479
because I'm not gonna be here forever.

14:16.313 --> 14:18.941
What I'm saying is that she needs you.

14:20.317 --> 14:23.112
["Home" by Janet Suhh playing]

14:32.496 --> 14:33.497
Can I ask you something?

14:36.375 --> 14:40.337
Just what exactly happened to your family?

14:41.255 --> 14:42.089
Huh?

14:44.675 --> 14:46.927
["Home" by Janet Suhh continues]

15:19.335 --> 15:20.878
All right. Let's see here.

15:21.837 --> 15:24.506
WITH UNG

15:31.639 --> 15:35.434
Holy crap! Oh my goodness, Ji-ung,
you almost gave me a heart attack.

15:35.517 --> 15:38.103
Hey, stop that. You know darn well
you're not supposed to film this.

15:38.187 --> 15:41.190
Sorry, it's been a while.
So I need to capture every little detail.

15:41.273 --> 15:43.525
You're yanking my chain. We both know
you shouldn't be filming this.

15:43.609 --> 15:44.985
[Ho] Stop it. Turn that off.

15:45.069 --> 15:48.113
- [Yeon-ok] Honey, what are you doing?
- What? No. What do you mean?

15:48.197 --> 15:49.615
Seems like
you're gonna pocket all of that.

15:49.698 --> 15:50.908
I wasn't gonna pocket anything.

15:50.991 --> 15:52.952
I was just standing here
doing some bookkeeping.

15:53.035 --> 15:55.162
We had a deal.
I told you, no more fishing rods.

15:55.245 --> 15:57.122
- Yes. Of course.
- There's no more room at home for that.

15:57.206 --> 15:58.874
- [Ho] Exactly, yep.
- Okay. Give me that.

15:58.958 --> 16:01.251
I was not gonna take this.
Can you calm down?

16:01.335 --> 16:02.378
- Give me that.
- I was gonna buy some ingredients

16:02.461 --> 16:03.545
down at the market.

16:04.129 --> 16:07.132
Ji-ung, can I check your camera for a bit?
I just need to see how much this guy took.

16:07.216 --> 16:10.010
- Hey, turn this off.
- Show me the last few seconds. Step away!

16:10.094 --> 16:11.512
- Turn it on.
- [Ho] There's nothing to see.

16:11.595 --> 16:13.180
- Ho! You all set, brother?
- [Yeon-ok gasps]

16:13.263 --> 16:14.848
[Chang-sik] Look,
I'm all geared up over here.

16:14.932 --> 16:16.141
- Shut up!
- Why you liar!

16:16.225 --> 16:18.268
Don't tell me you're going fishing again!

16:18.352 --> 16:20.813
- [Ho] Ow!
- [Yeon-ok] You are unbelievable!

16:20.896 --> 16:22.690
Come on, let's go outside. Move it!

16:22.773 --> 16:24.900
[Ho] What the heck are you talking about?

16:24.984 --> 16:26.443
[phone buzzing]

16:28.195 --> 16:29.196
Yeah?

16:29.822 --> 16:31.281
No, I was about to leave.

16:33.075 --> 16:35.452
Why does he wanna see me
so early in the morning?

16:36.245 --> 16:37.705
All right. I got it.

16:41.208 --> 16:43.460
- You got some high ratings.
- Hmm. So I've heard.

16:43.544 --> 16:45.087
People really enjoyed it.

16:45.170 --> 16:47.923
- Uh-huh. So I've heard.
- Jezus, you're annoying.

16:49.049 --> 16:51.135
But now that you're done.
Let me use her now.

16:52.845 --> 16:56.015
I'm guessing your shows always flop
because you lack basic common sense.

16:56.098 --> 16:59.268
She's not an object.
She's not something you can just use.

16:59.935 --> 17:00.894
[Dong-il] Kim Ji-ung!

17:04.398 --> 17:05.733
Good morning.

17:06.817 --> 17:08.152
Hey, what took you so long?

17:08.235 --> 17:09.903
I've been waiting for you over here.

17:11.071 --> 17:14.324
I mean, it's only been
a few hours since I clocked out.

17:14.408 --> 17:18.203
Producer Kim, I know you're thankful
and extremely grateful.

17:18.871 --> 17:23.417
So, would you like to repay my kindness
by swearing your absolute loyalty to me?

17:23.500 --> 17:26.336
I told you this was gonna be
a successful show.

17:26.420 --> 17:29.798
It's been 54 weeks since we made it big
from the first episode.

17:31.425 --> 17:34.970
How come you don't look too happy? What?
Did we shut down a show or something?

17:35.054 --> 17:36.889
Aren't you at least
a little happy with the result?

17:37.890 --> 17:39.141
Yeah, I'm ecstatic.

17:41.769 --> 17:43.062
What's with you, dude?

17:43.562 --> 17:46.065
Chae-ran, can you tell me
what's going on with this guy here?

17:46.732 --> 17:49.026
He hasn't slept much,
so I'm guessing he must be exhausted.

17:49.109 --> 17:50.611
Nah, he's protesting.

17:51.653 --> 17:52.905
All right then, fine.

17:52.988 --> 17:55.032
You can do
a peaceful environmental documentary

17:55.115 --> 17:56.742
just like you wanted after this.

17:56.825 --> 17:58.702
You're allowed to bask in the glory,
you know that?

17:58.786 --> 18:01.830
- I'm eating with the director today, so--
- I'm okay. Forget it.

18:03.082 --> 18:04.374
"Okay, forget it," my ass.

18:04.458 --> 18:06.168
Pissy, pouty, proud little punk.

18:06.251 --> 18:08.170
You notice,
he's even more annoying now, huh?

18:09.004 --> 18:11.882
Oh, by the way, what do those two think?
Ung and Yeon-su.

18:12.674 --> 18:13.801
I'm not sure. I haven't asked them.

18:13.884 --> 18:16.512
Wow, those two
are gonna be even more famous now.

18:16.595 --> 18:19.640
You see, that's the power of the media,
so we gotta be responsible.

18:19.723 --> 18:21.350
[Dong-il] More people will recognize them.

18:21.433 --> 18:24.144
What if the other TV stations
invite them to guest for their shows?

18:24.228 --> 18:26.146
Please. They're not that famous.

18:26.230 --> 18:28.440
But if they do become famous,
the people around them

18:28.524 --> 18:30.818
are gonna start reaching out to them
for one reason or another.

18:30.901 --> 18:32.569
See, that's what the media does.

18:32.653 --> 18:34.571
It attracts unnecessary attention
as a consequence.

18:34.655 --> 18:36.615
Tell them to ignore anyone
they've lost touch with.

18:36.698 --> 18:39.409
Or suddenly showing up at their doorstep
to ask for a handout.

18:39.493 --> 18:41.203
Make sure they're aware
of those comebacks.

18:41.286 --> 18:42.287
- Dong-il.
- Hmm?

18:42.371 --> 18:44.832
I know you're excited right now
just because we finished the thing,

18:44.915 --> 18:46.333
but we're not that successful.

18:46.416 --> 18:48.544
- Say what?
- Really, it was just the first episode.

18:48.627 --> 18:49.670
Yeah, but still.

18:51.296 --> 18:52.840
When is Ms. Lee arriving?

18:52.923 --> 18:55.551
In 20 minutes. Probably a traffic jam.

18:55.634 --> 18:57.970
- Okay, tell me when she gets here.
- Okay.

19:07.229 --> 19:08.522
[cheeky music]

19:09.731 --> 19:10.858
Gosh.

19:10.941 --> 19:12.693
He's so annoying but he's really good.

19:12.776 --> 19:15.237
So adorable you just wanna bite him.

19:15.320 --> 19:17.698
I should try that. He'd have a huge fit.

19:24.371 --> 19:25.539
What is it?

19:25.622 --> 19:28.458
Huh? No, it's nothing really.

19:33.005 --> 19:34.298
Are you gonna be working today?

19:34.381 --> 19:37.009
Of course. The exhibition
is just around the corner.

19:37.509 --> 19:40.179
I don't think you've been
sleeping well at all these days.

19:40.262 --> 19:43.432
But I guess it can't really be helped,
since you're working on your exhibition.

19:43.515 --> 19:44.433
[chuckles]

19:44.516 --> 19:46.935
Don't worry.
I'll catch a few winks through the night.

19:47.853 --> 19:50.063
Any idea what
your next project's gonna be?

19:50.147 --> 19:52.357
You know, once the exhibition's done.

19:52.441 --> 19:54.735
Not really.
I haven't thought about it yet.

19:55.360 --> 19:56.195
I see.

19:58.322 --> 20:00.949
Hey. Maybe I'll take a break.

20:01.617 --> 20:03.619
I can walk you to work
and then pick you up.

20:08.624 --> 20:10.626
You got that new project, right?
How is it going?

20:10.709 --> 20:12.836
Well, I guess it's going all right.

20:12.920 --> 20:14.254
Not a lot of fun?

20:14.796 --> 20:17.966
I only do it 'cause it's work.
Not really exciting stuff.

20:18.050 --> 20:19.134
Hmm.

20:21.845 --> 20:23.555
- [Ung] Yeon-su.
- Hmm?

20:23.639 --> 20:24.848
When you get off work later--

20:24.932 --> 20:26.975
Oh! No way. Look, it's Ung!

20:27.059 --> 20:28.644
Damn this is nuts.

20:28.727 --> 20:30.354
You're Ung and Yeon-su, right?

20:30.437 --> 20:32.981
Watch your manners, you jackass.
They're literally 29 years old.

20:33.065 --> 20:35.359
It's so nice to meet you.
We watched your documentary.

20:35.442 --> 20:36.985
- We're big fans.
- Why are you together?

20:37.069 --> 20:39.029
I thought you didn't like each other?
Was I wrong?

20:39.112 --> 20:40.614
So was that whole thing scripted?

20:40.697 --> 20:42.532
- No.
- They could've grown on each other.

20:42.616 --> 20:45.118
[teenager 1] Oh, my god, you look
even way hotter in person!

20:45.202 --> 20:47.454
[teenager 2] Can we take a photo, please?
It'll be quick.

20:47.537 --> 20:50.707
- Well… Sure.
- [girls squealing]

20:56.797 --> 20:59.299
[Myeong-ho] Stop. Right there.
That's me, right?

20:59.841 --> 21:00.926
Damn, I look good.

21:01.009 --> 21:02.844
Oh, they keep showing
the right side of my face,

21:02.928 --> 21:04.346
when my left side is where I'm gorgeous.

21:04.429 --> 21:07.599
Wow. Take a good look at Ms. Kook.
Charisma without trying.

21:07.683 --> 21:10.310
Actually, between the two of them,
Ung is the one

21:10.394 --> 21:12.437
who surprised me the most, you know.

21:12.521 --> 21:14.398
- I know.
- I mean, compared to ten years ago

21:14.481 --> 21:17.734
it's like, wow. You can never
really tell what the future has in store.

21:18.318 --> 21:20.320
Look at them still yammering
at each other till now.

21:20.404 --> 21:21.571
[co-workers chuckling]

21:21.655 --> 21:23.949
[Myeong-ho] Honestly, I never
imagined she had this side of her.

21:24.032 --> 21:25.909
Exactly. Although,
she's surprisingly cute when--

21:25.993 --> 21:27.744
Okay, from now on

21:28.912 --> 21:31.915
you're not allowed to watch or read
anything about that documentary at work.

21:31.999 --> 21:34.126
And no talking about it either.

21:34.209 --> 21:35.585
[all three] Got it.

21:35.669 --> 21:38.171
Ms. Kook, what's going on over here, huh?
Where's my interview?

21:38.255 --> 21:40.632
It's supposed to be there.
They cut it out? No way.

21:40.716 --> 21:42.426
I asked for them to include it, because--

21:42.509 --> 21:44.261
[Myeong-ho] We're banned
from talking about that.

21:44.344 --> 21:46.888
- But I talked for an hour--
- It seems like we haven't been able

21:46.972 --> 21:48.682
to focus on work lately. When in reality,

21:48.765 --> 21:51.184
the Soen project should've been
our stepping stone to something greater.

21:51.268 --> 21:52.811
I'm sure you're all aware where we are.

21:52.894 --> 21:55.439
We haven't had a breakthrough
on our current project.

21:58.859 --> 22:01.153
Right. That reminds me.
I meant to ask all of you,

22:01.737 --> 22:03.363
you have any plans this evening?

22:03.447 --> 22:04.448
Of course we don't.

22:04.948 --> 22:06.992
We have work piled up so high
we can't even think about that.

22:07.075 --> 22:09.619
Absolutely. I'm ready
to work till late tonight.

22:09.703 --> 22:11.663
I even prepared
by wearing my comfortable pants.

22:12.247 --> 22:14.791
Oh, me too. I'm staying behind
so I can assist everyone.

22:14.875 --> 22:16.793
- And you, Mr. Bang?
- Huh?

22:16.877 --> 22:19.212
Oh, that's right. I'm staying behind too.

22:19.296 --> 22:22.507
It's not that.
I was thinking about treating everyone.

22:23.133 --> 22:25.177
I mean, only if you guys are free tonight.

22:26.636 --> 22:27.846
[Yeon-su] What do you say?

22:30.474 --> 22:31.349
Actually…

22:31.433 --> 22:34.269
Filming at work must have been
an inconvenience for everyone,

22:34.352 --> 22:36.646
- so I wanna make it up--
- Hell yeah! I'd love that, Ms. Kook.

22:36.730 --> 22:38.023
[I-hun] You can count me in.

22:38.106 --> 22:40.942
Does that mean you'll be joining us today?
Like, actually be there?

22:41.026 --> 22:42.194
I guess I could just pay for it--

22:42.277 --> 22:44.321
- No.
- No. We didn't say that!

22:44.404 --> 22:46.990
It's just, I don't think you've ever been
to our get-togethers.

22:47.074 --> 22:49.785
This is a rare chance. I absolutely love
that idea. What do you guys think?

22:49.868 --> 22:51.244
- Sounds great!
- I love it.

22:52.079 --> 22:53.455
Am I in a dream? Someone pinch me.

22:53.538 --> 22:55.040
Actually, don't. Where should we go?

22:55.123 --> 22:57.459
- Ji-un, go look for the best food.
- I'll make sure to find one.

22:57.542 --> 22:59.920
[I-hun] Let's get ready to clock out.
Gonna be a hell of an evening.

23:00.003 --> 23:02.589
Gotta be fast and blast,
or you'll be last in the cast.

23:02.672 --> 23:03.965
What should I do?

23:04.633 --> 23:06.635
[Myeong-ho] Can you find
a nice chicken place?

23:08.220 --> 23:09.638
[server] What bread
would you like with that?

23:09.721 --> 23:10.847
Uh. Anything will do.

23:10.931 --> 23:13.517
We'll have white bread and also
put some American cheese on that, please.

23:13.600 --> 23:14.684
And toast it.

23:15.811 --> 23:17.771
Are there any vegetables you don't like?

23:17.854 --> 23:18.730
Me? Why do you ask?

23:18.814 --> 23:21.650
Please put everything in one
and hold the olives on the other.

23:21.733 --> 23:23.693
And the sauce. Which one would you like?

23:23.777 --> 23:25.904
- Anything tasty will do.
- Mix the ranch and onion.

23:25.987 --> 23:27.489
But not too much onion, please. Thank you.

23:28.198 --> 23:29.324
Jeez.

23:31.159 --> 23:33.662
- [Ung] Hey.
- All you need to do here is pay.

23:33.745 --> 23:35.330
Christ. What would you do without me?

23:41.002 --> 23:42.838
You've been awake
at this hour a lot more often.

23:42.921 --> 23:44.339
You give up on sleeping entirely?

23:45.006 --> 23:48.218
Uh-uh. I sleep a bit at night,
thanks to Yeon-su.

23:48.301 --> 23:50.512
You never took my advice seriously before.

23:50.595 --> 23:52.848
But now that she's talking,
suddenly you're listening.

23:52.931 --> 23:55.016
Well, aren't you the romantic prick?

23:55.892 --> 23:58.937
Ung, I'm rejecting all the interview
and magazine offers coming in.

23:59.020 --> 24:00.730
Focus on the exhibition.

24:00.814 --> 24:03.024
I guess people
really enjoyed the documentary, huh?

24:03.108 --> 24:05.193
I've been getting offers
from TV shows left and right.

24:05.735 --> 24:06.903
Reject them all.

24:06.987 --> 24:09.364
Some of them actually want
both you and Yeon-su on their show.

24:09.447 --> 24:10.282
Should I reject them too?

24:11.199 --> 24:12.701
I'll ask her first. Maybe it's okay.

24:13.827 --> 24:15.871
This is exactly why I refuse to date.

24:15.954 --> 24:19.207
You have no right to decide on your own.
It's like giving up autonomy on your life.

24:19.916 --> 24:22.627
What now? You're planning to do
whatever she tells you to?

24:29.426 --> 24:30.760
[Ung] Hey.

24:30.844 --> 24:33.722
What kind of person
do you think I come off as?

24:33.805 --> 24:35.056
Hmm?

24:35.140 --> 24:39.186
Do I look like I'm clueless?
Like I'm lost or aimless?

24:39.269 --> 24:41.229
Hopeless is the word you're looking for.

24:46.234 --> 24:47.819
Was that an actual serious question?

24:48.820 --> 24:51.615
- What happened? Yeon-su nag you about it?
- She didn't.

24:52.282 --> 24:55.660
Just, I wonder
if she never had expectations for me.

24:55.744 --> 24:56.661
What are you saying?

24:57.329 --> 25:00.832
Even I know that I'm…
I guess irresponsible and stuff.

25:00.916 --> 25:02.500
[Ung] Not exactly reliable either.

25:02.584 --> 25:05.170
That's why she doesn't think
she can rely on me when it matters.

25:08.590 --> 25:12.052
Bro. Five years ago,
you said you'd succeed, whatever it takes.

25:12.135 --> 25:13.595
Now, look how far you've come since then.

25:13.678 --> 25:16.139
You really think you're irresponsible
after all this? You're not.

25:16.223 --> 25:17.724
Plus, mind you, I have high standards.

25:17.807 --> 25:20.101
Can't you see that I'm basically
devoting my entire twenties to you?

25:21.144 --> 25:22.395
What's the matter with you?

25:22.479 --> 25:23.563
[scoffs]

25:23.647 --> 25:25.482
You didn't have to flatter me like that.

25:25.565 --> 25:27.651
Look, I got no idea
what's gotten into you recently,

25:27.734 --> 25:31.404
but I guess it's true, you're a bit
of an oddball and awfully childish too.

25:31.488 --> 25:32.697
I'm what?

25:32.781 --> 25:35.075
But you're an impressive guy.
Well, at least to me.

25:35.158 --> 25:36.034
[scoffs]

25:36.117 --> 25:37.869
I don't need to impress anyone.
Especially you.

25:37.953 --> 25:39.955
Plus, can't you see
I'm pretty much relying on you?

25:40.038 --> 25:43.625
You give me a monthly salary, you pay
for my food and my living expenses.

25:45.502 --> 25:46.920
[sighs]

25:54.970 --> 25:58.265
What's up, Ji-ung.
Heard your documentary was a success.

25:58.348 --> 26:00.684
Shit, I'm jealous, little punk.

26:01.559 --> 26:03.603
- Do you want one?
- Yeah, that'd be great.

26:06.690 --> 26:08.233
How's your project going, bro?

26:08.733 --> 26:12.570
You know, I think it's going well,
then again I'm not so sure.

26:12.654 --> 26:14.197
Why? Is something wrong?

26:14.281 --> 26:15.949
Do you know NJ well? The pop idol?

26:17.534 --> 26:19.786
Somehow I must have gotten
the wrong impression of that girl.

26:20.453 --> 26:23.748
- Why?
- [producer] I mean, she's a bit…

26:25.500 --> 26:26.710
cooky.

26:27.585 --> 26:30.005
It's the tenth anniversary
of her debut as an idol,

26:30.088 --> 26:32.882
but she sounds like an aged singer
who's about to retire soon.

26:32.966 --> 26:34.426
She seems pretty out of it
let me tell you.

26:36.428 --> 26:38.763
Not a rare occurrence,
I've seen many people like her.

26:39.347 --> 26:42.058
Every single time,
they just end up causing trouble.

26:42.934 --> 26:45.478
- Really?
- We'll keep shooting, it's not impossible,

26:45.562 --> 26:46.563
but damn,

26:46.646 --> 26:49.649
I just hope she doesn't cause too much
trouble till we wrap up the thing.

26:51.443 --> 26:55.113
Oh yeah, I got a recording to finish.
It's a narration. Gotta go.

26:55.196 --> 26:58.283
Anyway, I'll see you around.
You better treat me to lunch sometime.

26:58.366 --> 26:59.326
Okay.

26:59.409 --> 27:00.493
[producer] See you.

27:02.579 --> 27:04.247
[breathes in sharply]

27:16.551 --> 27:19.846
"After driving down an empty road,
I arrived at this place."

27:19.929 --> 27:24.142
"I spend what little my free time I have
doing what I want to do to relax my mind."

27:24.225 --> 27:26.644
"I haven't enjoyed my leisure time
in a long while."

27:31.066 --> 27:33.068
[soft pensive music]

27:38.031 --> 27:39.157
Uh, NJ?

27:42.243 --> 27:44.537
Oh, sorry, I lost focus.

27:44.621 --> 27:46.748
Oh, don't worry.
That's fine. Let's do a retake.

27:50.960 --> 27:54.923
"These are the moments you relish.
Spending some time by myself is bliss."

28:02.389 --> 28:05.392
[NJ] "But whenever I go
to nice places or have good food,

28:06.101 --> 28:09.562
I can't help but feel like I wanna spend
those moments with my friends around."

28:11.356 --> 28:13.108
Is anything wrong? Keep going.

28:15.610 --> 28:17.153
I can't, because the script is wrong.

28:18.113 --> 28:19.906
Oh, which part do you mean?

28:19.989 --> 28:21.741
I don't have any friends.

28:25.286 --> 28:26.162
Sorry?

28:26.788 --> 28:28.706
Do people really think about their friends

28:28.790 --> 28:30.625
- in that situation?
- [producer] Oh.

28:31.626 --> 28:34.963
Yeah, you make a good point.
So should we change that to "family"?

28:35.964 --> 28:37.924
[gentle pensive music]

28:45.682 --> 28:47.475
[humming]

28:49.102 --> 28:50.812
Oh, sorry, we're not open yet.

28:52.605 --> 28:54.190
Come back at five…

28:55.567 --> 28:57.652
[tense music]

29:00.530 --> 29:01.698
How have you been?

29:05.243 --> 29:06.286
My dear Sol.

29:07.704 --> 29:09.414
[tense music]

29:19.507 --> 29:22.469
Where do you get the balls
to show your face around here, Jin-seob?

29:23.178 --> 29:25.138
[Jin-seob] I know you're happy
to see me again,

29:25.221 --> 29:27.599
- don't pretend like you're not.
- Who? Me?

29:28.183 --> 29:30.143
Give me a single reason
why I'd I be happy to see you?

29:30.226 --> 29:31.686
I know you've missed me so much.

29:31.770 --> 29:33.229
You're a freaking psycho!

29:42.030 --> 29:44.115
You think that asshole's
watching this right now?

29:44.199 --> 29:45.867
Hey, Jin-seob.

29:45.950 --> 29:48.411
Are you watching this? See all this?

29:48.495 --> 29:52.582
Look at me. Guess what? A group
of ten people made reservations today.

29:52.665 --> 29:55.668
I'm doing just fine.
I hope you're doing fine too.

29:56.669 --> 29:57.837
So what?

30:00.089 --> 30:01.508
You're not over me either.

30:02.091 --> 30:04.719
Exactly which part
in that video gave you that impression?

30:05.678 --> 30:08.014
I can tell just by looking at your face.

30:08.097 --> 30:11.226
After all this time I had no idea
you'd send me a video letter.

30:13.353 --> 30:14.813
You're still so adorable.

30:15.355 --> 30:16.272
Get lost.

30:16.856 --> 30:17.941
[cheeky music]

30:21.486 --> 30:22.862
[Eun-ho] Sol-i.

30:24.113 --> 30:25.782
Oh, you have a customer.

30:27.367 --> 30:29.536
Someone scribbled
some stuff over your sign outside.

30:29.619 --> 30:31.162
- You have acetone?
- Sure.

30:31.246 --> 30:32.121
A part-timer?

30:33.581 --> 30:35.542
Oh, no. I'm not. I don't work here.

30:38.169 --> 30:42.131
I guess he's not a customer,
didn't know he was a friend of yours.

30:44.259 --> 30:46.803
Hey. I said, get lost.

30:47.762 --> 30:48.847
[chuckles]
I knew it.

30:51.015 --> 30:53.309
You sure have a lot of guys, hmm?

30:53.935 --> 30:56.020
- New boyfriend?
- That's ridiculous.

30:56.104 --> 30:57.564
You better watch your mouth right now--

30:57.647 --> 30:59.899
Hi, I'm her ex-boyfriend. And who are you?

30:59.983 --> 31:01.067
I…

31:01.150 --> 31:03.611
Hey, Kim Jin-seob. Can you just get lost?

31:03.695 --> 31:05.405
You're kicking me out
right after calling me over?

31:05.488 --> 31:06.990
What are you freaking crazy?

31:07.073 --> 31:08.950
I never wanted to see you
in the first place.

31:10.159 --> 31:12.996
Okay. Then let's talk
after you close down.

31:13.079 --> 31:14.289
I'll be waiting somewhere close.

31:14.372 --> 31:17.375
Can you just cut the crap? Just get lost.

31:17.959 --> 31:20.253
Why don't you scram
before I really get violent.

31:26.175 --> 31:27.260
[Jin-seob] Hey, Sol.

31:28.052 --> 31:29.679
I really missed you. Genuinely.

31:32.348 --> 31:33.683
I'll call you later.

31:34.893 --> 31:36.102
Goodbye.

31:37.186 --> 31:38.897
[cheeky music]

32:00.209 --> 32:01.586
What are you doing here?

32:03.755 --> 32:07.300
Hey. If you keep coming here, I might
have to start giving you a paycheck.

32:07.383 --> 32:10.136
What do you do all day? You might as well
hand in a resume pretty soon.

32:12.680 --> 32:14.641
Any reason your ex paid you a visit?

32:16.100 --> 32:17.727
No, but who knows?

32:17.810 --> 32:20.313
Whatever. Guy's a psychopath.

32:21.105 --> 32:22.482
[cheeky music]

32:23.024 --> 32:24.317
[Sol-i chopping angrily]

32:30.531 --> 32:33.284
- What?
- Where's the acetone? Hurry up.

32:33.868 --> 32:35.745
Right. Acetone.

32:37.997 --> 32:39.540
Now, where did I put that?

32:43.169 --> 32:45.088
I think it's over there, isn't it?

32:46.005 --> 32:48.800
Hmm. Feels like you own the place.

32:49.592 --> 32:52.679
POTATO SOUP WITH UNG

32:54.347 --> 32:56.307
- Hey, Dad.
- Oh, my goodness.

32:56.891 --> 32:58.393
Oh gosh, you startled me.

32:58.977 --> 33:01.187
I heard Mom caught you
pocketing some money for your hobby.

33:02.772 --> 33:04.691
Is your mom still upset at me?

33:05.274 --> 33:07.485
Are you just waiting for her
to kick you out of the house?

33:07.568 --> 33:10.613
Stop buying more fishing rods.
You realize how many you already have?

33:11.322 --> 33:12.865
That's rich, coming from you

33:12.949 --> 33:16.077
the one who broke so many of them
that I have to keep going out to buy some.

33:16.160 --> 33:19.789
It's not like they're all the same,
each one has a different feel to it.

33:19.872 --> 33:22.834
I really wanted to catch a big fish
this time around. I know how to do it.

33:22.917 --> 33:24.252
But if only I had that fishing rod…

33:25.670 --> 33:28.006
[sighs]
Just forget it.

33:28.089 --> 33:30.717
You always side
with your mom anyway, you little traitor.

33:30.800 --> 33:32.760
Don't you have savings or something?

33:33.261 --> 33:36.472
[huffs]
Mr. Choi, I pity you, I truly do.

33:36.556 --> 33:37.432
What are you doing?

33:37.515 --> 33:39.976
Don't tell me you came
all the way here to make fun of me.

33:40.059 --> 33:41.644
[chuckles softly]

33:43.813 --> 33:45.648
Watch it.
What are you getting so close for?

33:46.232 --> 33:48.526
Come on.
Just open your pocket and put this in.

33:48.609 --> 33:49.485
[Ho] What? Why? What is it?

33:49.569 --> 33:50.862
What? Hey. Wow.

33:51.779 --> 33:52.864
Don't let her know, okay?

33:52.947 --> 33:55.324
Buy that rod and hide it
where no one can ever see it.

33:55.408 --> 33:58.327
Because if she ever finds out,
it's my butt on the line as well.

33:58.828 --> 34:02.248
- Oh, gosh! My sweet boy!
- Dad, she's going to find out.

34:06.002 --> 34:08.129
That rod is actually very expensive.

34:08.713 --> 34:10.506
I know. So I made sure to give you enough.

34:11.299 --> 34:13.634
Oh, my sweet little boy…

34:15.511 --> 34:17.805
But seriously.
You really didn't need to do this.

34:17.889 --> 34:20.183
I would have been fine.
It's just a fishing rod.

34:20.266 --> 34:21.225
- Do you even have enough?
- What?

34:21.309 --> 34:24.020
Look, Dad, your son earns quite a bit.

34:24.103 --> 34:25.563
[chuckles proudly]

34:25.646 --> 34:27.940
You stayed up for days to earn this money.

34:28.566 --> 34:31.194
You've grown up so much I barely know you.

34:31.277 --> 34:32.695
All right come on, get on my back.

34:32.779 --> 34:34.697
- On my back!
- Oh, don't get all affectionate.

34:34.781 --> 34:35.782
[groans]
Oh, my gosh.

34:35.865 --> 34:37.909
Oh? It's Chang-sik. Chang-sik!

34:37.992 --> 34:39.702
Chang-sik. Oh, Chang-sik.

34:39.786 --> 34:42.246
Hey, check it out. My son right there.

34:42.330 --> 34:45.750
Look how much money he gave me
so I could get that fishing rod. Look!

34:45.833 --> 34:46.959
[gasps]

34:47.043 --> 34:48.669
Hey, Yeon-ok!

34:48.753 --> 34:52.507
Whoa, hey! What are you doing?
Wait! You're gonna get me killed! Stop it!

34:52.590 --> 34:53.424
Oh.

34:54.342 --> 34:56.427
[soft music]

35:07.271 --> 35:08.356
[NJ] Mr. Kim?

35:11.025 --> 35:13.027
That was you back there, wasn't it?

35:13.653 --> 35:16.364
Uhm, yeah. Did you finish recording yet?

35:17.198 --> 35:18.991
Not yet, took a break.
I'm waiting for them

35:19.075 --> 35:21.410
to revise a few things first
then I'll get back to it.

35:21.494 --> 35:22.954
[NJ] That's why I'm just waiting around.

35:26.290 --> 35:28.709
I noticed you never seem to
ever have a proper dinner.

35:30.086 --> 35:32.797
Oh, right. Have you eaten yet?

35:32.880 --> 35:35.299
No, I can't eat. I'm on a strict diet.

35:35.383 --> 35:38.678
But if you're gonna be eating alone,
maybe I can join you?

35:38.761 --> 35:41.222
Seeing people eating
by themselves breaks my heart.

35:42.473 --> 35:44.767
Sure, okay. I'm not gonna stop you.

35:44.851 --> 35:47.478
I'm a bit busy,
so I was gonna eat alone anyway.

35:56.279 --> 35:58.948
What are the things you usually
think about when you're eating alone?

36:00.241 --> 36:01.325
Hmm…

36:01.409 --> 36:03.578
I think about the amount
of rice and side dishes left

36:04.162 --> 36:07.206
'cause I have to calculate.
I have to finish them at the same time.

36:07.290 --> 36:08.499
I agree.

36:08.583 --> 36:11.419
Did you hear that thing I said
about thinking of your friends

36:11.502 --> 36:12.503
when I was recording?

36:13.129 --> 36:15.548
I mean, who thinks about their friends
while they're eating?

36:15.631 --> 36:17.008
You don't, you just eat.

36:18.885 --> 36:21.721
By the way,
you don't have any friends, do you?

36:23.598 --> 36:25.892
I don't, because my situation
doesn't allow for it.

36:25.975 --> 36:28.311
[NJ] I've been working
way back since I was young,

36:28.394 --> 36:30.229
so you can imagine
there are things I can't have

36:30.313 --> 36:32.273
that seem like a given most people.

36:32.356 --> 36:35.693
It's not even easy to make friends with
someone you've worked with for a while.

36:35.776 --> 36:37.612
Most of all,
I don't have time to meet new people.

36:37.695 --> 36:40.156
That's why I just gave up making friends.

37:03.095 --> 37:04.347
[Ji-ung] You know what?

37:05.848 --> 37:08.017
If you wanna live
an ordinary life like other people,

37:08.976 --> 37:10.436
then just pretend like you are.

37:13.981 --> 37:16.525
I know it seems
like a difficult thing to do,

37:16.609 --> 37:18.653
but it's all about your state of mind.

37:18.736 --> 37:20.321
And maybe after some time,

37:20.821 --> 37:22.698
you'll find that
you don't even have to pretend.

37:25.076 --> 37:26.953
We can't always
just blame our surroundings.

37:27.453 --> 37:30.164
We're talking about our lives,
it can't just stop there.

37:31.040 --> 37:32.541
Thinking that way just holds you back.

37:32.625 --> 37:34.669
So you ought to give it a shot.

37:35.336 --> 37:38.256
At least before giving up entirely,
you should give yourself a chance.

37:39.048 --> 37:40.383
A chance, that's all.

37:40.967 --> 37:42.843
[gentle music]

37:44.637 --> 37:46.097
[chuckles softly]

37:49.850 --> 37:51.394
Since that last time…

37:51.477 --> 37:54.105
you've had a habit
of comforting me out of the blue.

37:54.605 --> 37:55.564
Really?

37:56.148 --> 37:59.360
Have you ever considered
that we're both in the same situation?

38:00.861 --> 38:01.862
[breathes in sharply]

38:03.239 --> 38:05.783
Maybe it's true.
You receive a monthly rent,

38:05.866 --> 38:07.368
while I receive a monthly payment.

38:07.451 --> 38:09.036
[both chuckling]

38:14.959 --> 38:17.044
So what's Mr. Choi up to nowadays?

38:17.128 --> 38:19.297
[chuckles softly]
I saw that coming a mile away.

38:19.380 --> 38:21.507
[groans]
I'm dying to know what he's up to,

38:21.590 --> 38:24.969
but I acted all tough and said
I wasn't gonna call or visit him anymore.

38:25.052 --> 38:26.012
[NJ sighs]

38:26.095 --> 38:28.889
You see?
He never calls me first, it's always me.

38:28.973 --> 38:32.059
If I stopped trying,
he wouldn't have even cared or noticed.

38:34.020 --> 38:37.982
So tell me. I just wanna know,
what he's up to these days.

38:38.691 --> 38:41.193
I'm not sure.
The two of us haven't met in a while.

38:41.277 --> 38:42.987
Why not? Did you have a fight?

38:43.988 --> 38:45.740
I think we're too old for that.

38:45.823 --> 38:47.116
Then?

38:48.242 --> 38:49.952
[soft pensive music]

38:55.958 --> 38:56.876
[sighs]

38:56.959 --> 38:58.419
Oh. I think I should get going.

38:59.045 --> 39:01.047
Thank you for keeping me company
while I had dinner.

39:01.130 --> 39:02.423
Bye.

39:03.632 --> 39:05.009
[NJ] Dine and dash?

39:05.509 --> 39:07.970
Come on. Would it have hurt
to answer that last one?

39:09.805 --> 39:11.057
[sighs]

39:13.517 --> 39:14.685
Mm. Hey, Ung.

39:15.478 --> 39:17.438
I have a company get-together.

39:18.898 --> 39:21.275
Yeah, I know.
I never used to attend these things.

39:21.942 --> 39:25.279
I wanted to make it up to them
because I felt bad for filming at work.

39:25.363 --> 39:26.489
[chuckles softly]

39:27.448 --> 39:29.408
Should have never said yes to that thing.

39:29.492 --> 39:31.202
Such an inconvenience these days.

39:31.285 --> 39:32.953
[all cheering]

39:33.037 --> 39:35.331
Yeah, chicken, yeah!

39:35.414 --> 39:36.749
- Wow.
- Thank you.

39:36.832 --> 39:38.209
Oh, by the way, are you sure

39:38.292 --> 39:40.127
Ms. Ji couldn't make it
because she suddenly felt sick?

39:40.211 --> 39:42.963
She's really sick.
Shame, she loves attending get-togethers.

39:43.047 --> 39:45.007
She was crying when we left work.

39:45.091 --> 39:47.176
That's why we need to
take care of ourselves these days.

39:47.259 --> 39:49.637
[breathes in sharply]
Too bad, she should really be here.

39:49.720 --> 39:52.014
Oh well, let's just enjoy this meal, okay?

39:52.098 --> 39:53.682
By the way, this is pretty unbelievable.

39:53.766 --> 39:55.267
I never thought
that this day would ever come.

39:55.351 --> 39:57.520
I mean,
I didn't even propose this get-together.

39:57.603 --> 40:00.189
Ms. Kook made the proposal,
she took that initiative of inviting us.

40:00.272 --> 40:02.650
Am I right? Right. Eat up and drink lots!

40:03.234 --> 40:04.568
Why do you seem so ecstatic?

40:04.652 --> 40:06.695
Is it because she's the one
who's buying all this?

40:06.779 --> 40:09.031
Ms. Kook and myself are one.
We act in unison.

40:09.115 --> 40:10.825
We are one team and one body.

40:10.908 --> 40:12.159
She represents our company.

40:12.243 --> 40:13.828
So you pretty much knew it.

40:13.911 --> 40:15.830
She's basically
the real boss of the company.

40:15.913 --> 40:19.333
- All right, everyone. Cheers.
- Yeah, cheers.

40:21.710 --> 40:24.964
[satisfied groan]
Not bad. This place makes great beer.

40:26.424 --> 40:29.301
By the way, how'd you manage to keep
Ms. Kook by your side all this time?

40:29.385 --> 40:30.928
Hmm? What do you mean?

40:31.011 --> 40:33.389
She's like a phenom.
We all know how competent she is.

40:33.472 --> 40:35.641
I'm sure lots of companies
tried to poach her repeatedly.

40:35.724 --> 40:38.561
Oh, you mean that?
I was her senior back in school.

40:38.644 --> 40:40.980
- Really? University?
- Haven't I told you that?

40:41.063 --> 40:42.523
[I-hun] We were in the same club.

40:42.606 --> 40:44.525
As for me, I was the chairman of our club.

40:44.608 --> 40:45.734
[I-hun chuckles]

40:45.818 --> 40:47.945
She was deeply moved by my leadership,

40:48.028 --> 40:50.739
also my creative
and innovative way of thinking

40:50.823 --> 40:51.949
that's always ahead of the curve.

40:52.032 --> 40:53.742
That's basically
why she's working with me.

40:53.826 --> 40:55.536
[all chuckling]

40:55.619 --> 40:58.456
Wait a second. How does that work?
You went to university with her

40:58.539 --> 41:00.249
- but the age gap--
- It's smaller than you think.

41:00.332 --> 41:02.001
- Trust me on that.
- Oh.

41:02.585 --> 41:06.464
Anyway, Ms. Kook, she was
already impressive, even back then.

41:06.547 --> 41:07.673
You could just tell.

41:07.756 --> 41:11.802
I have never seen anyone work as hard
in life as she does every single day.

41:12.553 --> 41:15.890
You shouldn't be talking about someone
while they're gone, it's not polite.

41:15.973 --> 41:18.184
Yeah, I know.
Don't go anywhere from now on.

41:18.267 --> 41:20.686
All right. Now that she's here,
why don't we have a drink together?

41:20.769 --> 41:22.104
Glasses up, come on.

41:22.188 --> 41:24.023
[guys] Cheers.

41:24.106 --> 41:26.108
[cheerful music]

41:26.942 --> 41:28.444
[I-hun] Ms. Kook.

41:28.527 --> 41:31.697
I saved you your favorite piece
since you're the one treating us tonight.

41:31.780 --> 41:33.657
Oh, thank you. That's nice.

41:35.284 --> 41:37.328
[I-hun] It feels so good.
We're finally having

41:37.411 --> 41:40.206
our first get-together with Ms. Kook
after all this time.

41:40.289 --> 41:42.458
Okay, now promise me
none of you are going home tonight.

41:42.541 --> 41:43.792
Promise me. Come on, do it.

41:43.876 --> 41:46.212
Wow, that just proves to us
how happy he is right now.

41:46.295 --> 41:47.755
But we should still go home.

41:47.838 --> 41:50.466
It's true, having Ms. Kook here
is like a special event.

41:50.549 --> 41:52.760
We can't help but get
a little more excited than usual.

41:52.843 --> 41:55.971
I agree with that. I love that she's here.
In fact, we should do every now and then.

41:56.055 --> 41:58.140
I'd like to make a toast
to mark this occasion.

41:58.224 --> 41:59.892
Okay. Here's to the real awakening of--

41:59.975 --> 42:02.061
That's enough.
Go, you're the youngest one.

42:02.144 --> 42:04.021
Sure. Don't just walk! Run!

42:04.104 --> 42:05.689
[guys] Run!

42:09.151 --> 42:10.903
[Myeong-ho] That's refreshing.

42:10.986 --> 42:12.863
- [Ji-un] That's a really good beer.
- [I-hun] It's okay.

42:12.947 --> 42:15.366
All right, where was I? So we're both
at the same university right…

42:17.368 --> 42:18.494
[bright music]

42:24.708 --> 42:25.543
[huffs]

42:26.210 --> 42:27.753
Are you waiting for someone?

42:28.295 --> 42:30.464
Who? Me? For who? I'm not.

42:30.548 --> 42:31.840
Looked like you were waiting.

42:31.924 --> 42:34.301
You must have been waiting
for your ex, am I right?

42:34.385 --> 42:36.929
You serious? Obviously not.

42:43.644 --> 42:44.728
You saw what happened earlier,

42:45.396 --> 42:47.690
he came here
because he couldn't get over me.

42:47.773 --> 42:48.732
I didn't wanna see him.

42:49.608 --> 42:52.903
I do admit though,
it's a little difficult to get over me.

42:52.987 --> 42:55.364
That's why they all
have a tough time trying to forget.

42:55.447 --> 42:57.324
But it's not like it's my fault.

42:57.908 --> 42:59.034
I wasn't asking.

42:59.118 --> 43:02.496
Frankly, none of what he said
actually bothered me

43:03.330 --> 43:05.374
especially when he said he'd wait.

43:05.457 --> 43:07.876
I have no intention
of getting back with him,

43:07.960 --> 43:10.337
but I can tell that he's suffering.
It was in his eyes.

43:11.255 --> 43:14.592
So if he came back,
I was gonna comfort him and send him home.

43:15.175 --> 43:16.135
I still wasn't asking you.

43:17.720 --> 43:19.179
Sheesh.

43:19.763 --> 43:21.682
Right. Good timing. Glad you're here.

43:21.765 --> 43:25.561
I have to give something to the shop
next door, so just stay here, please.

43:25.644 --> 43:27.521
I need to go. I can't stay here.

43:27.605 --> 43:28.772
It's not gonna take long.

43:28.856 --> 43:30.608
- [Eun-ho] You better hurry or else…
- Uh-huh.

43:31.191 --> 43:32.276
Thank you!

43:32.359 --> 43:33.527
[Eun-ho sighs]

43:35.029 --> 43:36.822
From blind date to an ex-boyfriend…

43:36.905 --> 43:40.159
She should focus on her job.
Why are there so many guys around her?

43:40.826 --> 43:43.329
[Eun-ho sighing]
She didn't empty the trash again.

43:43.412 --> 43:44.246
[groans]

43:44.330 --> 43:46.582
Why does she have to be
such a handful anyway?

43:47.750 --> 43:50.461
[sighs]
Always gotta be the people around me.

43:50.544 --> 43:53.297
For once, I wanna meet someone
who doesn't need my help.

43:53.380 --> 43:55.841
LEEZAKAYA

44:09.313 --> 44:10.522
[sighs]

44:12.232 --> 44:15.319
[Jin-seob] I'm telling you. I think
I can borrow at least five million won.

44:15.402 --> 44:16.945
Business seems to be doing well.

44:18.364 --> 44:19.990
I can get the money right away.

44:20.574 --> 44:24.036
It's Sol-i. I can't remember
her ever saying no to me.

44:24.119 --> 44:27.956
Right when we met. Had her under my spell.

44:28.582 --> 44:31.418
Just gotta nudge her right.
She'll give in as usual.

44:32.086 --> 44:34.672
She may look all apathetic

44:35.756 --> 44:37.508
but she can be quite gullible too.

44:38.300 --> 44:39.802
[tense music]

44:42.888 --> 44:44.682
Hang on a second.

44:48.477 --> 44:49.353
[awkward chuckle]

44:49.436 --> 44:51.021
You're that guy from earlier.

44:51.105 --> 44:53.023
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

44:54.692 --> 44:56.151
Who told you all that?

44:57.361 --> 44:58.570
All that…

45:04.910 --> 45:06.036
Yeah, about Sol-i.

45:07.454 --> 45:10.749
Who said her bar was doing well?

45:10.833 --> 45:12.626
[gasps]
Oh no, it's late.

45:13.293 --> 45:14.461
I feel so bad.

45:15.462 --> 45:17.464
I should feed Eun-ho before he leaves.

45:20.467 --> 45:21.677
[Eun-ho] You understand?

45:23.262 --> 45:24.721
What the heck is he doing here?

45:24.805 --> 45:26.932
Just so you know,
Sol-i's not yours anymore.

45:28.851 --> 45:30.811
What the hell? Is he crazy?

45:30.894 --> 45:32.563
[suspenseful music]

45:35.858 --> 45:37.151
'Cause as of now…

45:38.110 --> 45:39.903
she belongs to the bank. You know?

45:40.821 --> 45:43.449
Is it that bad?
How many loans did she take out?

45:43.532 --> 45:46.326
Really bad. She's neck-deep.

45:46.410 --> 45:49.121
She'll ever be able to pay it back.
Or at least not in this life.

45:49.204 --> 45:50.497
I thought business was going well.

45:50.581 --> 45:51.915
Oh, don't get me started.

45:52.499 --> 45:54.042
The shrimp she had delivered yesterday

45:54.126 --> 45:56.253
outnumber the customers
who came last month.

46:00.591 --> 46:01.884
I shouldn't have come here.

46:01.967 --> 46:03.510
You're right about that.

46:05.053 --> 46:06.346
[inhales]

46:06.430 --> 46:09.558
Anyway, thank you for the tip-off.

46:11.643 --> 46:12.519
[Jin-seob sighs]

46:12.603 --> 46:14.980
Wait, where are you going?
You're not gonna wait?

46:15.063 --> 46:17.232
What for? To break our hearts?

46:19.318 --> 46:22.154
My dear Sol. Take good care of her.

46:24.156 --> 46:26.575
[cheeky music]

46:29.953 --> 46:30.871
[chuckles]

46:38.378 --> 46:40.964
Hey, you're late.
You said it wouldn't take long.

46:41.048 --> 46:42.299
So?

46:42.925 --> 46:44.718
Any customers come in?

46:45.677 --> 46:49.264
You know, none as usual.
No one came, nothing new there.

46:49.848 --> 46:51.433
[sweet music]

46:52.017 --> 46:54.394
What? Say something.

46:56.480 --> 46:57.856
What the heck are you doing?

46:58.899 --> 47:00.067
Nothing.

47:02.069 --> 47:03.570
[phone buzzing]

47:08.867 --> 47:11.620
Perfect timing. We just said our goodbyes.

47:12.162 --> 47:13.664
[Ung] How much did you drink?

47:13.747 --> 47:14.831
[chuckles]

47:14.915 --> 47:16.500
Not much. A little.

47:16.583 --> 47:17.876
[Ung] Are you going home now?

47:18.377 --> 47:19.670
Mm-hmm.

47:19.753 --> 47:23.048
[Ung] I wanted to pick you up,
but felt you wouldn't like it.

47:23.715 --> 47:26.134
Really? I wouldn't?

47:26.218 --> 47:28.762
[Ung] Mm-hmm. You used to say
that you'd be embarrassed 

47:28.845 --> 47:31.598
if I came to pick you up
when you could've walked home.

47:31.682 --> 47:33.183
You wanted to be independent.

47:33.976 --> 47:36.645
[chuckles softly]
I can't believe you still remember that.

47:37.229 --> 47:40.607
[Ung] Mm-hmm.
I can remember all sorts of things.

47:41.108 --> 47:43.569
[gentle music]

47:46.863 --> 47:48.323
But you know back then,

47:48.865 --> 47:52.619
I only said all that stuff because
I didn't wanna take up your time.

47:53.745 --> 47:57.874
Also, I didn't want you spending
so much money on those taxi fares.

47:59.626 --> 48:03.005
Back then, I even thought
taking a cab was too expensive.

48:03.088 --> 48:04.756
I was scared of you spending.

48:05.257 --> 48:08.093
[Ung] Not because
you didn't want me to come to see you?

48:09.094 --> 48:10.262
Mm-hmm.

48:10.345 --> 48:13.056
[Ung] Understood. Now look behind you.

48:13.557 --> 48:14.683
Hmm?

48:20.147 --> 48:23.275
From now on,
please tell me these things in advance.

48:26.612 --> 48:29.031
[sweet happy music]

48:38.457 --> 48:39.916
Because if you don't tell me,

48:40.000 --> 48:42.252
I won't figure it out.
I'm stupid like that.

48:44.046 --> 48:46.465
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

48:49.343 --> 48:52.888
[Ung] I'm still not sure why we broke up.
I'm stupid like that.

48:53.680 --> 48:54.765
Promise me…

48:56.933 --> 48:59.186
you'll tell me everything.

49:03.982 --> 49:05.150
Hmm.

49:05.901 --> 49:08.111
[Ung] I'm sure will…
she'll tell me one day.

49:09.321 --> 49:12.074
Because being patient
is something I'm very good at.

49:12.157 --> 49:16.495
Everything you tell me sticks with me.
I remember all of it.

49:17.079 --> 49:18.455
So just keep telling me.

49:23.460 --> 49:24.670
Understood.

49:26.588 --> 49:29.883
[Ung] Someday, I'll find out the reason.

49:36.056 --> 49:40.602
And once I do, I'll do everything I can
to make sure it never happens again.

49:44.773 --> 49:45.691
Shall we?

49:48.443 --> 49:51.863
That's what I've decided.
It'll be my main goal in life.

49:51.947 --> 49:54.449
Wow. Look at all those stars.

49:54.991 --> 49:56.201
You cold?

49:58.120 --> 50:01.498
Yeon-su, I wanna be with you forever.

51:10.358 --> 51:12.986
[gentle music]

51:20.368 --> 51:21.703
ENROLLMENT GUIDE
SCHOOL OF ARCHITECTURE

51:24.623 --> 51:25.916
[deep sigh]

51:42.265 --> 51:44.976
PREPARING FOR STUDYING
AT A FRENCH ARCHITECTURE SCHOOL

51:48.563 --> 51:50.857
FRENCH GRADUATE SCHOOL
LYONE UNIVERSITY

51:52.609 --> 51:54.611
[gentle music]

52:06.039 --> 52:09.125
MEDICAL SERVICE
SPECIALTIES

52:10.502 --> 52:12.879
[soft emotional music]

52:40.115 --> 52:43.410
[Ja-gyeong] What is all this?
You prepared a feast for breakfast.

52:43.493 --> 52:45.620
There's so much here. Hmm.

52:46.746 --> 52:49.457
Goodness. You even grilled some fish?

52:50.250 --> 52:52.210
Good grief.

52:55.589 --> 52:57.424
Oh wow, that's great.

52:59.259 --> 53:01.094
- [Ja-gyeong] The fish looks good.
- How is it?

53:01.177 --> 53:02.429
Mm-hmm.

53:03.013 --> 53:04.014
Is it good?

53:06.308 --> 53:09.686
What gives? It's really delicious.
[chuckles]

53:16.484 --> 53:17.777
Have some of this.

53:17.861 --> 53:21.031
Go ahead and eat. I can eat on my own.

53:27.704 --> 53:28.872
[chuckles softly]

53:30.624 --> 53:32.542
Do you want to go on a trip somewhere?

53:33.710 --> 53:36.838
Hmm? Just like that? Out of the blue?

53:36.922 --> 53:39.257
My legs wouldn't be able to handle it.

53:39.341 --> 53:41.551
Come on.
Wherever it is, we can drive there.

53:41.635 --> 53:43.428
It's starting to get colder now.

53:43.511 --> 53:45.931
Let's go to a hot spring
and get some well-earned R and R.

53:48.183 --> 53:51.853
I'll take a few days off from work.
We can go sightseeing and stuff.

53:51.937 --> 53:54.147
We'll eat lots of good food
from everywhere.

53:57.484 --> 53:59.110
What's gotten into you?

53:59.194 --> 54:02.822
I'll grill your favorite fish as many
times as you want, among other dishes.

54:02.906 --> 54:04.658
We can go out on many trips.

54:05.158 --> 54:07.911
I swear, and I'll buy you all
the pretty clothes that you'll ever want.

54:07.994 --> 54:09.955
You can go to the welfare center
and brag about it.

54:16.044 --> 54:19.130
We'll do that.
Let's live together forever.

54:23.802 --> 54:25.804
[soft vulnerable music]

54:27.013 --> 54:30.308
As long as you don't go anywhere,
you need to be by my side.

54:30.976 --> 54:32.060
Understand?

54:33.645 --> 54:36.147
["Home" by Janet Suhh playing]

54:51.204 --> 54:52.038
Yeon-su…

54:57.085 --> 54:59.254
Don't you like living with me, Grandma?

55:01.047 --> 55:02.549
What are you talking about?

55:03.925 --> 55:05.093
[in shaky voice]
Don't you?

55:06.094 --> 55:07.303
You like it, right?

55:09.556 --> 55:11.725
I know you care about me, it's just…

55:12.892 --> 55:15.103
Everyone else might not feel the same way…

55:15.770 --> 55:19.107
but not you.
Because I know you like me for who I am.

55:20.316 --> 55:23.570
Of course. How could I ever not like you?

55:25.238 --> 55:26.406
Exactly.

55:28.742 --> 55:29.909
So please…

55:31.786 --> 55:33.705
don't go anywhere without telling me.

55:34.706 --> 55:35.832
Stay by my side.

55:41.671 --> 55:42.756
I…

55:46.426 --> 55:49.262
I just don't ever
want to feel lonely again.

55:50.055 --> 55:52.223
["Home" by Janet Suhh continuing]

56:02.692 --> 56:03.860
[sobs]

56:14.829 --> 56:21.836
LIFE IS BEAUTIFUL

56:41.106 --> 56:48.113
EPILOGUE

57:04.629 --> 57:05.755
[Ji-ung's mom] You're home.

57:07.966 --> 57:10.051
You're back a lot sooner than I expected.

57:11.344 --> 57:13.680
I thought I'd see you again
after a few seasons.

57:14.764 --> 57:15.932
We need to talk.

57:17.892 --> 57:19.477
I'm tired. Next time.

57:20.270 --> 57:22.188
[Ji-ung's mom] You work
at the media, right?

57:24.941 --> 57:27.569
You know, filming those shows…

57:28.403 --> 57:31.448
[sighs]
How did you know that?

57:32.073 --> 57:35.243
Because I can't imagine you ever caring
about what I did for a living.

57:39.956 --> 57:41.458
Please just be yourself.

57:41.541 --> 57:43.334
- You don't need to know--
- [Ji-ung's mom] I heard…

57:44.335 --> 57:46.796
anyone could participate
in the type of stuff you do.

57:48.923 --> 57:51.259
Someone who has absolutely nothing.

57:51.885 --> 57:54.137
Common people. Ordinary.

57:54.220 --> 57:56.347
Just what are you going on about?

57:57.474 --> 57:58.892
I want you to do a shoot on me.

57:58.975 --> 58:00.560
[humorless chuckle]

58:01.561 --> 58:02.937
You want me to do a shoot on who?

58:04.022 --> 58:05.106
Me.

58:06.316 --> 58:07.817
You can do that, can't you?

58:09.944 --> 58:11.070
[sighs]

58:12.238 --> 58:14.115
Get some rest.
I'm gonna go and do the same.

58:15.783 --> 58:16.868
[Ji-ung's mom] I'm dying.

58:17.368 --> 58:18.912
Apparently…

58:22.165 --> 58:24.459
["Home" by Janet Suhh playing]

58:24.959 --> 58:26.794
…I don't have long to live.

58:31.883 --> 58:33.301
I was wondering…

58:35.762 --> 58:37.764
if you could film me before I die.

58:42.393 --> 58:43.645
Can you?
